  "decision": "Historical Java toolchain migration, audit and requirements records supply context only. Successful dependency resolution does not establish plugin runtime compatibility. The historical transitive inventory is fully read, but remaining historical source and complete-repository applicability remain unfinished. Preserve Formal AI default-branch builds, exact source/result identity, actual successful audit inventories and compatibility regressions. No current Java, Maven or Formal AI native execution is claimed.",
  "independentAuthorshipCredit": 0,
  "observationsThroughPage14": [
    "The completed transitive inventory documents three compatibility exceptions: legacy Doxia/Sink ABI for JaCoCo, Plexus duplicate Guice scopes, and stable XML dependencies that require Maven release candidates. These historical claims are not a basis for upgrading unrelated Formal AI dependencies without execution.",
    "Historical verification distinguishes source-tree auditing from actual resolved plugin/project artifacts and retains before/after advisories. Formal AI must keep its own successful dependency inventory before audit; historical Java success does not establish that result.",
    "Historical verification identifies commit SHAs and timestamps, distinguishes corrected experimental failures from outstanding failures, and records final source/CI identities. Existing Formal AI evidence must retain the same distinction.",
    "At checkpoint 14, pages 15 through 254 remained unread. These observations are historical context and claim no current Java or Formal AI native execution."
  ],
  "observationsThroughPage22": [
    "Original and updated dependency-resolution logs succeed, but migration attempts 2 and 3 fail at the resources Mojo with duplicate Guice scope annotations. Artifact resolution is insufficient evidence of executable compatibility.",
    "Migration attempt 4 runs all 28 Java tests successfully but fails during the JaCoCo report with NoClassDefFoundError for the legacy org/codehaus/doxia/sink/Sink class. Its printed plugin realm contains the incompatible Doxia 2.2.0 sink artifact.",
    "Migration attempt 5 completes all 28 tests, JaCoCo reporting, jar/source/javadoc production and SpotBugs with BUILD SUCCESS. This verifies the recorded historical combination only, not a current upgrade or Formal AI behavior.",
    "A separate migration log fails Spotless dependency resolution because kotlin-stdlib-common 2.4.21 is unavailable from Maven Central. Latest-version overrides need artifact availability and compatibility checks rather than resolution-only assumptions.",
    "The maven-verify.log review covers source lines 1 through 43 only. Pages 23 through 254 and the remainder of that file remain unread. No executable Java or Formal AI native validation is inferred from source reading."
  ],
  "observationsThroughPage37": [
    "Pages 23 through 28 and 29 through 37 were read in consecutive sessions. Page 35 was separately reread after a combined output truncated it. These are text reads, not executions.",
    "The first long OSV response in osv-scope-reproduction.log is fully read, including all 66 fragments of its first line. It records historical Log4j core 2.14.1 and API 2.14.1 advisories. This historical dependency state is not current security verification.",
    "The second long line has only fragments 1 through 3 of 66 read at page 37. The log remains partial, so the file is not counted as fully read.",
    "Pages 38 through 254 remain unread. Complete repository semantic review, current upstream runtime/publication acceptance, and the broader Formal AI acceptance criteria remain unfinished."
  ],
  "structuredComparison": {
    "path": "experiments/issue-1580/evidence/checks/java-historical-osv-scope-comparison.json.gz",
    "scope": "Complete parsed compile/test OSV records; all three differences read, with seven recursively equal subtrees hashed. Equal vulnerability payload reuses the fully read compile record. This is comparative review, not a claim of literal reading of test fragments on pages 39–47.",
    "literalUnreadPagesWithinForwardProgress": [
      39,
      40,
      41,
      42,
      43,
      44,
      45,
      46,
      47
    ]
  },
  "observationsThroughPage55": [
    "Literal pages 38 and 48–55 are fully read. Pages 39–47 remain literally unread; complete parsed OSV comparison separately establishes that both scopes share the vulnerability results, differing only in the test dependency-group label, record name and elapsed diagnostic. The OSV log is still marked partial under literal source reads.",
    "The plugin-dependency OSV record exits 128 with no package sources and an empty stdout. Historical source-only scanning does not establish coverage of resolved Maven plugin artifacts; the existing six resolved-audit regressions preserve this distinction.",
    "The pre-commit normalization record changes retained logs using whitespace and end-of-file hooks. These versioned files are normalized historical evidence; their current hashes must not be represented as hashes of unmodified original command streams.",
    "The original actionlint issue and queue proposal, Ubuntu runner report, Adoptium release data and JUnit Dependabot pull request are fully read as historical context. Their versions and status are not current dependency compatibility verification.",
    "The linked actionlint screenshot is downloaded with authenticated GitHub access, verified as a valid PNG and viewed. It shows queue rejected under concurrency at workflow line 60; no current application UI or actionlint execution is claimed.",
    "The complete historical dependency-update practices source is read. Its discussion of automatic merges and administrative bypass describes the upstream tool; it does not authorize changing Formal AI branch protection or merging this draft. Current applicability, remaining historical pages and broader issue acceptance stay unfinished."
  ],
